    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A steppe khaganate that ruled the Carpathian basin from 568, with a mounted warrior elite over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a> and others.</li><li>It drew huge gold payments from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 626, but failed to take it.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avar-ring">Avar Ring</a> in 795–796; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> are last mentioned in 822.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> are generally credited with bringing the iron stirrup into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strategikon-of-maurice">Byzantine Strategikon</a> advised Roman cavalry to copy their equipment.</p></aside>
    </section>

